// The first draft used short, summary-like nodes. These expanded scene models keep
// geography, time, motive and prior choices explicit so every beat earns the next.
Object.assign(stories[0],{length:'11 substantial scenes · 3 endings',hook:'Three days before the Aurora Awards, a stolen master track pulls you between Jungkook, San, and the friend who warned you not to trust either of them.',start:'a0',setup:{kicker:'THREE NIGHTS. ONE STOLEN SONG.',title:'Afterglow Protocol',body:'You are an independent documentary editor hired to film the final seventy-two hours before the Aurora Awards. Jungkook is returning with the first song he produced entirely alone. San is opening the broadcast with a rival stage built around the same rare melody. When Jungkook’s master file vanishes during rehearsal, the network quietly blames San—and your camera may be the only witness that can prove what really happened.',stakes:'Find the thief before the live show, protect the people who trusted you, and decide which heart—if any—gets yours.',warning:'A fictional romance-mystery inspired by public performance personas.'},nodes:{
 a0:{chapter:'CHAPTER 1 · THE BLACKOUT',place:'AURORA ARENA · TUESDAY, 11:47 PM',who:'Jihyo',transition:'Your first night on the documentary ends with the entire arena losing power.',context:'You are filming from the sound booth when the monitors die mid-rehearsal. In the dark, somebody brushes past your shoulder. Thirty seconds later the emergency lights return: Jungkook’s encrypted master drive is gone, San’s silver ring lies beside the console, and the broadcast director orders every exit locked.',text:'Jihyo catches your wrist before security reaches you. “That ring is too convenient. Someone wants us looking at San instead of the booth.” She glances toward Jungkook, alone on the dark stage. “You have the only camera that was recording.”',choices:[['Give Jihyo your memory card and work as a team.','a1',{trust:2},'You choose Jihyo over a dramatic solo investigation.'],['Keep the footage and check on Jungkook first.','a1',{jk:2},'You protect the person who just lost his most personal work.'],['Photograph the ring and find San before security does.','a1',{san:2,clue:1},'You decide the obvious suspect deserves a warning.']]},
 a1:{chapter:'CHAPTER 1 · THE BLACKOUT',place:'SERVICE CORRIDOR B · 12:06 AM',who:'You',transition:'Security seals the main floor. Jihyo leads you through a costume passage behind the stage.',context:'Your previous choice changes who walks beside you, but the destination is the same: a blind spot behind the sound booth. Your footage shows a hooded figure leaving at 11:46. They are carrying a pink staff credential and limping on the left side.',text:'A new message lights your phone before you can enlarge the frame.',type:'phone',messages:[['unknown','DELETE THE VIDEO. THE SONG ISN’T WORTH WHAT HAPPENS NEXT.'],['you','Who is this?'],['unknown','ASK WHY JUNGKOOK’S PASS OPENED THE BOOTH. ASK SAN WHAT HIS RING WAS DOING THERE.']],choices:[['Send screenshots to Jihyo immediately.','a2',{trust:2},'You refuse to let the threat isolate you.'],['Reply: “Meet me. Come alone.”','a2',{bold:2},'You bait the blackmailer into making another move.'],['Say nothing and trace the number through Felix.','a2',{clue:2},'You keep the threat quiet until you know who sent it.']]},
 a2:{chapter:'CHAPTER 2 · TWO ALIBIS',place:'EMPTY MAIN STAGE · 12:24 AM',who:'Jungkook',transition:'The unknown number goes silent. A stagehand tells you Jungkook refused to leave until he searched the arena himself.',context:'You find him beneath ten thousand empty seats, replaying the same eight bars through one earbud. The missing track was written during a year when he could not finish anything. Tomorrow’s rehearsal is the first time anyone was supposed to hear it.',text:'“My pass did open the booth,” he admits before you ask. “At eleven thirty. I went to leave you a copy of the documentary score.” He offers the earbud. “I know how that sounds. But I didn’t steal my own song.”',choices:[['Take the earbud and ask him to walk you through every minute.','a3',{jk:2,clue:1},'You answer vulnerability with patience, not suspicion.'],['Ask for his pass and verify the access log first.','a3',{clue:2},'You keep the investigation ahead of the chemistry.'],['Call Jihyo so the interview has a witness.','a3',{trust:2},'You make sure neither of you has to rely on blind faith.']]},
 a3:{chapter:'CHAPTER 2 · TWO ALIBIS',place:'ARENA ROOFTOP · 1:02 AM',who:'San',transition:'Jungkook’s access log proves he entered early—but someone used his pass again during the blackout. Then security radios that San has been found on the roof.',context:'Rain needles the concrete. San stands beside an open maintenance panel, his stage shirt soaked through. He says his ring fell off while he was following someone from the booth. Inside the panel, you find a severed fiber line and one strand of metallic pink thread.',text:'“I could have run when they found the ring,” San says. “I stayed because whoever did this wanted my name attached to it.” He holds out his phone. At 11:44, he received the same threat you did.',choices:[['Believe him and let him join the investigation.','a4',{san:2,clue:1},'You decide two matching threats outweigh one planted ring.'],['Take the phone but keep San at a distance.','a4',{clue:2},'You accept the evidence without offering trust yet.'],['Tell him about Jungkook’s duplicated pass.','a4',{san:1,jk:1},'You share the whole picture and ask him to do the same.']]},
 a4:{chapter:'CHAPTER 3 · THE PINK THREAD',place:'24-HOUR EDIT SUITE · WEDNESDAY, 2:18 AM',who:'Felix',transition:'Jihyo gets everyone past security by claiming your documentary needs an emergency reshoot. She takes you, Jungkook, and San to Felix’s off-site edit suite.',context:'Felix recovers seven damaged seconds from your camera: the hooded figure is wearing a network credential and carrying a garment bag from Jennie’s styling department. A reflection shows a bracelet printed with the Aurora broadcast logo.',text:'“The threat came through the network’s internal messaging relay,” Felix says. “And the stolen song never left this building. Someone copied it to a hidden server downstairs.”',choices:[['Go downstairs with Jihyo and Felix—quietly.','a5',{trust:2,clue:2},'You choose the careful route and keep the team together.'],['Ask Jennie about the garment bag before accusing anyone.','a5',{clue:2},'You follow the physical evidence to the person who can explain it.'],['Split up: Jungkook takes the server, San takes the credential list.','a5',{jk:1,san:1,bold:1},'You trust both men with separate pieces of the case.']]},
 a5:{chapter:'CHAPTER 3 · THE PINK THREAD',place:'WARDROBE LEVEL · 3:05 AM',who:'Jennie',transition:'The hidden server requires a producer’s key. The pink thread leads everyone to wardrobe, where Jennie is still repairing the live-show looks.',context:'Jennie recognizes it immediately: not from her clothes, but from the emergency credential lanyards issued to senior producers. She opens the garment bag from the footage. Inside is a duplicate of Jungkook’s jacket and a pair of shoes altered to create a limp.',text:'“This isn’t sabotage between artists,” Jennie says. “It’s a storyline. Rival steals comeback. Two fandoms tear each other apart. Ratings triple.” She shows you a contract addendum authorizing the network to use backstage documentary footage—including yours.',choices:[['Tell the whole group what the contract says.','a6',{trust:2},'You choose transparency even though it implicates your own footage.'],['Hide your name in the contract until you understand it.','a6',{secret:2},'Fear wins a small, consequential victory.'],['Ask Jennie to help turn wardrobe into a trap.','a6',{bold:2,clue:1},'You convert the planted evidence into bait.']]},
 a6:{chapter:'CHAPTER 4 · DAYLIGHT',place:'CONVENIENCE STORE · 4:12 AM',who:'Jihyo',transition:'With rehearsal suspended until noon, Jihyo marches everyone across the street for food and a decision.',context:'The six of you crowd around plastic tables under fluorescent light. Jungkook admits the stolen chorus contains a melody San once improvised during a charity stage. San never asked for credit. That resemblance is what made the network’s fake rivalry believable.',text:'Jihyo sets two ramyeon cups in front of you. “One problem at a time. First: are you still making the documentary, knowing they planned to use it against us?”',choices:[['Keep filming, but give the group final approval.','a7',{trust:3},'You turn the camera from a weapon into shared evidence.'],['Put the camera away and become part of the story.','a7',{heart:2},'You choose the people in front of you over the film.'],['Keep filming secretly until you capture the producer.','a7',{bold:2,secret:1},'You risk everyone’s trust for evidence no one can deny.']]},
 a7:{chapter:'CHAPTER 4 · DAYLIGHT',place:'YOUR PHONE · 9:16 AM',who:'Group chat',transition:'Four hours later, you wake on the edit-suite couch to thirty-two notifications.',context:'The network announces that San has withdrawn for “personal reasons.” He has not. Someone used his manager’s account. At the same time, a private demo of Jungkook’s song begins spreading online.',type:'phone',messages:[['Jihyo','Nobody posts. Nobody leaves alone.'],['San','My manager did not send that statement.'],['Jungkook','The leak is an older demo. Only three people had it.'],['Felix','Found the hidden server. It wipes itself at 8 PM.'],['Jennie','Then we give them a better story before eight.']],choices:[['Stay with San and publicly challenge the false withdrawal.','a8',{san:3,trust:1},'You protect San when the planted narrative becomes public.'],['Help Jungkook replace the leaked demo with a live performance.','a8',{jk:3,trust:1},'You help Jungkook reclaim the song on his terms.'],['Follow Jihyo and Felix to copy the hidden server.','a8',{trust:3,clue:2},'You prioritize proof that can protect everyone.']]},
 a8:{chapter:'CHAPTER 5 · DRESS REHEARSAL',place:'AURORA ARENA · 6:38 PM',who:'You',transition:'By sunset the plan is set: perform the song live, lure the producer into wiping the server, and project the deletion log onto every press-room monitor.',context:'Jennie dresses you as a production assistant so you can reach the control room. Jihyo wears the only earpiece connected to everyone. San is supposed to appear halfway through Jungkook’s stage, revealing that the “stolen” melody was always a gift between artists.',text:'At the elevator, Jungkook and San arrive from opposite corridors. Both know this may be the last private minute you get before the trap begins.',choices:[['Tell Jungkook: “Whatever happens, finish your song.”','a9',{jk:3},'You give Jungkook the certainty he has been giving everyone else.'],['Tell San: “Don’t disappear just because they wrote you out.”','a9',{san:3},'You ask San to stay—in the show and with you.'],['Pull them both into the world’s most awkward team hug.','a9',{trust:3},'You choose solidarity and make both men laugh at the worst possible time.']]},
 a9:{chapter:'CHAPTER 5 · THE CONTROL ROOM',place:'BROADCAST CONTROL · 7:56 PM',who:'The Producer',transition:'The live stage begins. While Jungkook sings the first verse, Jennie’s borrowed credential gets you into the control room.',context:'The senior producer is waiting. He admits the scheme without looking away from the monitors: the leak, the ring, the fake withdrawal. Then he reveals the final trap. If you copy the server, an automated injunction kills the broadcast and buries the evidence for years. If you stay quiet, he restores both artists’ stages and deletes your contract.',text:'“You wanted a story,” he says. “I’m offering you an ending where everyone keeps their career.” In your earpiece, Jihyo asks if you are in position. Onscreen, San steps into the light beside Jungkook.',choices:[['Trigger the copy and let the broadcast go dark.','a10',{truth:4,trust:1},'You decide a protected lie is still a lie.'],['Send the confession audio to Jihyo but do not trigger the server.','a10',{strategy:4,clue:1},'You choose a quieter weapon and keep the stage alive.'],['Pretend to accept, then hand control to Felix remotely.','a10',{bold:3,clue:2},'You make the producer believe he won long enough to expose himself.']]},
 a10:{chapter:'FINALE · LIVE',place:'AURORA STAGE · 8:03 PM',who:'Jihyo',transition:'Your decision hits the arena in real time.',context:'The screens flicker. The crowd falls silent. Jihyo walks onstage with your camera in her hand—not as evidence against one person, but as a record of every choice the group made together.',text:'“They wanted a rivalry,” she tells you through the earpiece. “Give them the truth.” You have one final cut to make.',choices:[['Air the documentary with everyone’s consent.','end',{together:4},'You make the truth a collective decision, not your personal victory.'],['Protect the private moments; air only the producer’s confession.','end',{care:4},'You expose the crime without turning vulnerability into content.'],['End on the shared performance and release the investigation tomorrow.','end',{music:4},'Tonight belongs to the song. Tomorrow belongs to accountability.']]}
}});
Object.assign(stories[1],{length:'6 substantial scenes · 3 endings',setup:{kicker:'EVERY PORTRAIT HIDES A SECOND FACE.',title:'Velvet Alibi',body:'You arrive at Han Arts University on a scholarship your mother never told you she applied for. On your first night, your roommate disappears after leaving a voice note about the Nocturne Society. Mingyu’s family founded it. Hyunjin swears he joined only to destroy it. Both are lying—but not about the same thing.',stakes:'Find your roommate before the Founder’s Gala and decide whether to expose the institution or inherit its secrets.',warning:'A fictional campus-noir romance.'},nodes:{
 v0:{chapter:'NIGHT ONE · THE BELL',place:'HAN ARTS DORMITORY · 11:58 PM',who:'Rosé',transition:'You have been on campus for six hours when the sealed bell tower begins playing a melody nobody recognizes.',context:'Your roommate Ara is missing. Her phone is on her desk, still recording. Rosé, the musician across the hall, identifies the melody as a cipher used in an old student protest.',text:'The recording ends with Ara whispering, “Ask the boy in the velvet jacket.” At that moment Mingyu knocks, worried. Through the window, you see Hyunjin crossing the quad in the same dark velvet.',choices:[['Tell Rosé everything and search as a pair.','v1',{trust:2},'You choose a witness before choosing a suspect.'],['Follow Mingyu to the photography lab.','v1',{mingyu:2},'You follow the man whose family name is carved over the front gate.'],['Follow Hyunjin into the locked gallery.','v1',{hyunjin:2},'You chase the person already running from you.']]},
 v1:{chapter:'NIGHT ONE · THE PORTRAIT',place:'FOUNDERS GALLERY · 12:21 AM',who:'Hyunjin',transition:'Every route leads to the closed gallery: Rosé breaks a window, Mingyu has a key, or Hyunjin leaves the door open behind him.',context:'Behind a portrait of the university’s founder is a fresh photograph of Ara. On the back: COME ALONE TO THE GALA. Hyunjin admits he painted over the portrait last week and found dozens of names hidden beneath it—including yours, dated before you were born.',text:'“I joined Nocturne to find who destroyed my sister’s career,” he says. “Ara joined to find out why your mother vanished from this school.”',choices:[['Believe the motive, not the man. Ask for proof.','v1b',{clue:2},'You give Hyunjin one chance to substantiate his story.'],['Call Mingyu and demand the Nocturne archive.','v1b',{mingyu:2,bold:1},'You force the golden boy to choose a side.'],['Take the photograph to campus security.','v1b',{trust:1},'You try the official door before breaking another rule.']]},
 v1b:{chapter:'DAY TWO · THE WARNING',place:'STUDENT RADIO BOOTH · 8:10 AM',who:'Rosé',transition:'At dawn, campus security returns the photograph and labels Ara a runaway. Rosé pulls you into the radio booth before the dean can find you.',context:'An anonymous caller hums the bell-tower melody backward. Rosé reverses the recording and uncovers a sentence from your mother: “The archive is beneath the place where they teach us to be quiet.” The library opens in twenty minutes. Someone is already waiting outside the booth.',text:'“We can keep chasing their clues,” Rosé says, “or make enough noise that they have to chase us.”',choices:[['Broadcast Ara’s voice note and ask the campus for help.','v2',{truth:2,trust:1},'You turn a private disappearance into a public question.'],['Leave silently through the equipment hatch.','v2',{clue:2},'You protect the one clue Nocturne does not know you solved.'],['Text Mingyu and Hyunjin the same meeting place.','v2',{bold:2},'You force both suspects into the same room.']]},
 v2:{chapter:'DAY TWO · THE ARCHIVE',place:'BENEATH THE LIBRARY · 3:40 PM',who:'Mingyu',transition:'The reversed message leads below the library. Mingyu uses his family key after making you promise not to mistake access for innocence.',context:'The archive proves Nocturne has traded scholarships for silence for thirty years. Your mother was the last student who tried to expose it. Ara found her unfinished evidence and staged her disappearance to force the society into moving its records.',text:'Mingyu’s name appears on tonight’s induction list. “My father thinks I’m taking his place,” he says. “I’m actually giving you access. If you can still trust me.”',choices:[['Take Mingyu’s hand and enter the gala as his guest.','v2b',{mingyu:3},'You accept the risk hidden inside his perfect plan.'],['Ask Hyunjin to create a distraction at the gallery.','v2b',{hyunjin:3},'You trust the artist to make the institution look at itself.'],['Bring Rosé and broadcast from the student radio booth.','v2b',{trust:3,truth:2},'You make sure the truth cannot disappear with one person.']]},
 v2b:{chapter:'DAY TWO · THE INVITATION',place:'COSTUME BASEMENT · 8:45 PM',who:'Mingyu',transition:'The gala requires a mask, an invitation, and a lie convincing enough to survive the first dance. Your chosen ally brings all three.',context:'Tucked inside the invitation is a note in Ara’s handwriting: DO NOT RESCUE ME. STEAL THE LEDGER. It changes the plan. She did not disappear to be found; she disappeared to put the original evidence within reach.',text:'“Once we enter, the doors lock until midnight,” Mingyu says. Across the room, Hyunjin paints a copy of the founder’s seal while Rosé wires a microphone into your collar. “If you want out, choose now.”',choices:[['Enter as Mingyu’s partner and keep the microphone live.','v3',{mingyu:2,truth:1},'You combine his access with Rosé’s safety net.'],['Enter with Hyunjin’s forged invitation.','v3',{hyunjin:2,bold:1},'You trust art to pass as authority.'],['Send Rosé to the radio booth before you go in.','v3',{trust:2,truth:2},'You make sure someone outside can hear the doors lock.']]},
 v3:{chapter:'THE FOUNDER’S GALA',place:'NOCTURNE HALL · 11:30 PM',who:'Ara',transition:'Masked students waltz beneath the library while your chosen ally gets you past the door.',context:'Ara is not a prisoner. She is onstage, pretending to accept Nocturne’s offer so she can reach the original ledger. When the founder orders her to name the student who helped her, she looks directly at you.',text:'The fire doors lock. The ledger is on the podium. Your mother’s testimony is queued in Rosé’s radio booth. You have time for one move.',choices:[['Steal the ledger and run with Ara.','vend',{care:4},'You choose your friend’s safety and physical proof.'],['Signal Rosé to broadcast every name.','vend',{truth:4},'You make secrecy impossible, whatever it costs.'],['Let your chosen boy confess his family or society role publicly.','vend',{heart:4},'You ask love to look like accountability.']]}
}});
Object.assign(stories[2],{length:'6 substantial scenes · 3 endings',setup:{kicker:'TAKE FORTY. THIS TIME, TELL THE TRUTH.',title:'Second Take, First Love',body:'You are the rookie writer of a romance drama that should have launched your career. Instead, a prop meteor destroys the café set during the finale—and you wake at 7:03 AM on the same disastrous day. V remembers fragments. Joshua remembers the feelings. Sana believes you immediately. The loop resets whenever you deliver the scripted confession.',stakes:'Finish the episode without lying about what you want—or remain inside the perfect romance forever.',warning:'A fictional time-loop romantic comedy.'},nodes:{
 s0:{chapter:'TAKE 38 · AGAIN',place:'SOUNDSTAGE 7 · 7:03 AM',who:'Jisoo',transition:'A meteor crashes through your café set at 8:44 PM. You wake thirteen hours earlier with plaster still in your hair.',context:'Producer Jisoo is the first person you test. Before she can speak, you recite her breakfast order and predict a lighting failure. She believes you only after the light explodes exactly on cue.',text:'“The reset happens after the heroine’s confession,” Jisoo says. “That means either the universe hates romance, or it hates your dialogue.”',choices:[['Tell Sana, your best friend and leading lady.','s1',{trust:2},'You choose the person who knows when you are lying.'],['Test whether V remembers the kiss scene.','s1',{v:2},'You look for recognition in your leading man.'],['Ask Joshua to help rewrite the finale.','s1',{josh:2},'You turn to the second lead who always fixes your pages.']]},
 s1:{chapter:'TAKE 39 · THE RULES',place:'WRITERS’ ROOM · 10:15 AM',who:'Yunjin',transition:'By lunch, your small conspiracy has mapped thirty-eight failed versions of the day.',context:'Yunjin notices every loop ends on a sentence you wrote before production began: “I have always chosen you.” The problem is that you no longer know who “you” means—or whether romance is the ending you want.',text:'“Then stop polishing the lie,” Yunjin says. “Change what happens before the confession. Make a choice the old script cannot predict.”',choices:[['Give V the quiet scene he asked for months ago.','s1b',{v:3},'You listen to the actor instead of the ratings notes.'],['Restore Joshua’s deleted ending.','s1b',{josh:3},'You give the second lead permission to change the story.'],['Write Sana a future that does not revolve around either man.','s1b',{trust:3},'You center the friendship the script treated as background.']]},
 s1b:{chapter:'TAKE 39 · THE MEMORY TEST',place:'PROP ROOFTOP · 1:20 PM',who:'V',transition:'To make a choice the loop cannot predict, you move rehearsal to a rooftop set nobody has used since episode three.',context:'V finishes the new scene without looking at the page. Then he quotes a line from loop seventeen—a version of the day he should not remember. Joshua arrives carrying coffee you only asked for in loop nine. The reset is leaking into them through emotion, not facts.',text:'“I don’t remember the days,” V says slowly. “I remember missing you in all of them.” Joshua looks at you as if he understands exactly what that costs.',choices:[['Tell both men the truth about every loop.','s2',{truth:2,trust:1},'You stop managing their feelings and give them the facts.'],['Ask V what he remembers when he sees you.','s2',{v:2},'You follow the emotional memory back to him.'],['Ask Joshua why he keeps bringing the same coffee.','s2',{josh:2},'You notice the quiet ritual that survived thirty-nine endings.']]},
 s2:{chapter:'TAKE 40 · OFF SCRIPT',place:'EMPTY CAFÉ SET · 6:50 PM',who:'Sana',transition:'The rewritten pages change the day. For the first time, the prop meteor fails to launch on schedule.',context:'Sana finds a hidden production note inside the meteor rig: LOOP UNTIL THE ENDING TESTS WELL. The network’s experimental audience system has been resetting the simulation, and Jisoo has unknowingly been feeding it each new take.',text:'“We can film the ending they want and leave,” Sana says, “or break the system and lose the whole show. But this time, you decide before the cameras decide for you.”',choices:[['Film one honest confession, even if it is imperfect.','s2b',{heart:3},'You keep the romance but remove the lie.'],['Destroy the loop system and the footage with it.','s2b',{bold:3},'You choose reality over the project that trapped you.'],['Turn the finale into a live behind-the-scenes broadcast.','s2b',{truth:3},'You let the audience see every failed version.']]},
 s2b:{chapter:'TAKE 40 · THE PRODUCER',place:'CONTROL BOOTH · 8:10 PM',who:'Jisoo',transition:'Thirty-two minutes before the reset, Jisoo unlocks the control booth and shows you the audience system.',context:'Every choice has a predicted satisfaction score. V’s perfect confession ranks first. Joshua’s improvised exit ranks second. Choosing Sana or yourself is marked INVALID ENDING. Jisoo can disable the score, but doing so means the cameras will keep rolling with no approved script.',text:'“I spent all day producing the ending,” Jisoo says, hand over the switch. “I should have been protecting the people trapped inside it.”',choices:[['Disable the score and keep the cameras rolling.','s3',{truth:2},'You want the audience to see an ending no model approved.'],['Disable everything and finish in private.','s3',{care:2},'You refuse to turn escape into another piece of content.'],['Feed the system a deliberately impossible ending.','s3',{bold:2},'You decide the fastest way out is to break its idea of a story.']]},
 s3:{chapter:'FINAL TAKE',place:'CAFÉ SET · 8:42 PM',who:'You',transition:'Two minutes before the meteor is supposed to fall, the cameras begin rolling by themselves.',context:'V stands at the scripted mark. Joshua waits by the exit. Sana holds the system’s power cable. Jisoo gives you the smallest nod. Nobody speaks the cue line.',text:'For forty days, the scene demanded that you choose the most satisfying ending. Now it asks for the truest one.',choices:[['Choose the person your earlier actions kept returning to.','send',{romance:4},'You allow love, but refuse the predetermined version of it.'],['Choose Sana and build a different show together.','send',{trust:4},'You choose the relationship that survived every reset.'],['Choose yourself and pull the power.','send',{self:4},'You end the story before it can define you again.']]}
}});

// Presentation-night editions: recognizable romantic tropes, frequent choices,
// and direct relationship routes inspired by mobile visual-novel pacing.
Object.assign(stories[0],{title:'Three After Midnight',genre:'Office Romance · Love Triangle',length:'7 scenes · 3 endings',hook:'One office party. Three men in your messages. By sunrise, everybody will know who you chose.',tags:['office crush','three-way texting','one magical night'],cast:[['Jungkook','BTS','Your sweet office crush','Quietly attentive; remembers your coffee order.'],['San','ATEEZ','The playful new strategist','Flirty, fearless, and impossible to ignore.'],['Mingyu','SEVENTEEN','Your demanding team lead','Sharp at work, surprisingly gentle after hours.'],['Jennie','BLACKPINK','Your glamorous work bestie','The friend who sees every crush before you do.'],['Rosé','BLACKPINK','The accidental matchmaker','Sincere, romantic, and holding the karaoke mic.']],setup:{kicker:'ONE PARTY. THREE TEXTS. NO SAFE CHOICE.',title:'Three After Midnight',body:'You plan to attend the company party for one polite hour. Then your longtime crush Jungkook asks you to dance, charming new hire San starts flirting like it is his job, and intimidating team lead Mingyu smiles at you for the first time in six months.',stakes:'Survive karaoke, a neon-lit night out, and three confessions—then choose who gets the final dance and the morning after.',warning:'A playful fictional office-romance fantasy. All characters are adults.'},start:'o0',nodes:{
o0:{chapter:'CHAPTER 1 · THE PARTY',place:'MIRAE MEDIA ROOFTOP · 8:12 PM',who:'Jennie',transition:'Friday begins with a deadline and ends beneath a hundred fairy lights on the company rooftop.',context:'Jennie zips you into the emergency party outfit she keeps behind her desk. Across the rooftop, Jungkook pretends not to look at you. San openly looks at you. Mingyu stops mid-sentence when you walk in.',text:'You have three problems: the one you have wanted for a year, the one who wants you already, and the one who acts like wanting anything is against company policy.',choices:[['Ask Jungkook for the first dance.','o1',{jk:3},'Your office crush finally gets the hint.'],['Let San steal you for the first song.','o1',{san:3},'You reward confidence with confidence.'],['Bring Mingyu his usual drink.','o1',{mingyu:3},'You surprise the man who notices everything.']]},
o1:{chapter:'CHAPTER 1 · KARAOKE',place:'NEON NOTE KARAOKE · 10:06 PM',who:'Rosé',transition:'When the rooftop closes, Rosé persuades everyone to continue the party two blocks away.',context:'Jennie keeps score whenever one of the three men finds an excuse to sit beside you. By the second round, your cheeks are warm from one celebratory cocktail—or from all the attention.',text:'Duet rule! Choose your partner. Pretending you suddenly lost your voice is not an option.',choices:[['Jungkook: a soft love song.','o2',{jk:2},'He harmonizes perfectly and never looks away.'],['San: a shameless dance track.','o2',{san:2},'He changes the lyrics to include your name.'],['Mingyu: a dramatic ballad.','o2',{mingyu:2},'He complains—then sings directly to you.']]},
o2:{chapter:'CHAPTER 2 · THREE MEN ARE TYPING',place:'YOUR PHONE · 11:18 PM',who:'Friday night',transition:'You step into the hallway for water. Before you can return, your phone lights up three times.',context:'All three men are still inside the same karaoke room. None of them has considered how suspicious it looks to text you simultaneously.',type:'phone',messages:[['Jungkook','You looked happy tonight. I have wanted to tell you that for a while. Are you okay out there?'],['San','Escaping without me? Rude. Meet me downstairs and I will show you the best bar in Seoul 😉'],['Mingyu','You have had enough of Rosé’s punch. Drink the water I left by your coat. That is an instruction.'],['you','Do all three of you know you are texting me right now?'],['San','I do now.'],['Jungkook','…three?'],['Mingyu','Come back inside. We need to discuss boundaries.']],choices:[['Text Jungkook: “Come find me.”','o3',{jk:3},'You choose the kind message that calmed your heart.'],['Text San: “You have ten minutes to impress me.”','o3',{san:3},'You accept his playful invitation.'],['Text Mingyu: “That sounded jealous.”','o3',{mingyu:3},'You challenge his commanding tone.']]},
o3:{chapter:'CHAPTER 2 · THE NIGHT OUT',place:'EULJIRO NIGHT MARKET · 11:46 PM',who:'You',transition:'Jennie declares karaoke over. Everyone spills into the bright streets in search of food.',context:'Jungkook offers his scarf. San buys hotteok and steals the first bite. Mingyu trades your cocktail for warm tea. When your heel catches on the curb, three hands reach for you.',text:'For one ridiculous second, the sidewalk becomes a romantic standoff. Jennie hides her laugh behind both hands.',choices:[['Take Jungkook’s hand and keep his scarf.','o4',{jk:3},'His thumb brushes yours, then stays.'],['Link arms with San and steal the hotteok back.','o4',{san:3},'He grins like this was always the plan.'],['Let Mingyu steady you—and stay close.','o4',{mingyu:3},'His stern expression finally breaks.']]},
o4:{chapter:'CHAPTER 3 · TAKE CARE',place:'CONVENIENCE STORE PATIO · 12:22 AM',who:'Jennie',transition:'A sudden winter rain traps everyone beneath a convenience-store awning.',context:'You are tipsy enough to laugh at everything but steady enough to choose. All three men argue—politely, then not so politely—about who should take you home.',text:'A sensible best friend would call you a taxi. Unfortunately, I want to see who wins.',choices:[['Ask Jungkook to walk you home slowly.','o5',{jk:4},'You choose softness and your oldest crush.'],['Ask San about the best bar in Seoul.','o5',{san:4},'You choose one more adventure.'],['Tell Mingyu he can take responsibility.','o5',{mingyu:4},'The tension is no longer professional.']]},
o5:{chapter:'CHAPTER 3 · THE CONFESSION',place:'CHEONGGYECHEON · 1:07 AM',who:'Your chosen man',transition:'Instead of going home, the two of you walk beside the stream until the city noise disappears.',context:'The jokes fade first, then the office titles. He tells you the exact moment he began noticing you: a rainy coffee run, an elevator argument, a meeting where you defended someone who was not there.',text:'Tomorrow we can pretend this was the party talking. But I would rather tell you the truth tonight.',choices:[['Kiss him before he overthinks it.','o6',{heart:4},'You answer without another meeting.'],['Make him say exactly what he wants.','o6',{bold:3},'You have waited too long for vague feelings.'],['Admit you chose him all night.','o6',{heart:3,trust:2},'The confession becomes mutual.']]},
o6:{chapter:'FINALE · AFTER MIDNIGHT',place:'PENTHOUSE LOUNGE · 2:03 AM',who:'You',transition:'The rain returns. He brings you to the quiet guest lounge in his building for tea and a dry coat.',context:'City lights cover the windows. Your phone holds two unread goodnight messages from the men you did not choose. The man beside you offers to call a car. You are completely sober now.',text:'The night can end at the elevator—or become the beginning of the office romance everyone will notice on Monday.',choices:[['Stay and close the door behind you.','oend',{stay:5},'You choose a private, magical night together.'],['Share one kiss, then plan a real date.','oend',{slow:5},'You choose anticipation.'],['Invite everyone to breakfast.','oend',{chaos:5},'You choose friendship before Monday’s chaos.']]}}});

Object.assign(stories[1],{title:'My Best Friend’s Brother',genre:'Forbidden Romance · Summer',length:'6 scenes · 2 endings',hook:'Your summer with Jihyo has one rule: her older brother is off-limits. His best friend was never mentioned.',tags:['best friend’s brother','beach house','two boys'],cast:[['Jihyo','TWICE','Your ride-or-die best friend','Protective, honest, and terrible at subtlety.'],['Bang Chan','Stray Kids','Her off-limits older brother','Responsible, warm, and always taking care of everyone.'],['Joshua','SEVENTEEN','His charming best friend','Gentle manners hiding a competitive streak.'],['Sana','TWICE','Your chaos-loving confidante','Romantic, observant, and full of bad advice.']],setup:{kicker:'HER BROTHER IS OFF-LIMITS. HIS BEST FRIEND ISN’T.',title:'My Best Friend’s Brother',body:'Jihyo invites you to spend two weeks at her family’s beach house. You expect movies and terrible cooking. You do not expect her older brother Bang Chan to look unfairly grown-up—or his best friend Joshua to claim the room across from yours.',stakes:'Survive shared breakfasts, beach games, and almost-kisses. Then tell your best friend which boy has your heart.',warning:'A fictional summer romance. All characters are adults.'},start:'b0',nodes:{
b0:{chapter:'DAY ONE · THE RULE',place:'JIHYO’S BEACH HOUSE · 4:30 PM',who:'Jihyo',transition:'Your best friend picks you up with the windows down and one suspiciously specific house rule.',context:'Chan carries your suitcase upstairs. Joshua appears wearing an apron and offers you the first strawberry from his cake. Both volunteer to teach you to surf.',text:'Before this becomes one of your romance novels: my brother is off-limits. Joshua is technically available, but if he breaks your heart, I will bury him in the sand.',choices:[['Tease Chan about the rule.','b1',{chan:3},'His ears turn pink. Jihyo notices.'],['Ask Joshua if he always bakes for strangers.','b1',{josh:3},'He says you stopped being a stranger years ago.'],['Promise this is a girls’ trip.','b1',{friend:2},'A sincere promise that lasts six minutes.']]},
b1:{chapter:'DAY THREE · CHEMISTRY',place:'HAEUNDAE BEACH · 2:15 PM',who:'Joshua',transition:'Two days of shared breakfasts lead to an intensely competitive beach afternoon.',context:'Chan teaches you to balance on a surfboard, hands steady at your waist. Joshua dives through the sand to save your volleyball shot. Jihyo watches both interactions with suspicion.',text:'Your best friend’s brother is trying very hard not to look jealous. Should I make it easier for him—or harder?',choices:[['Tell Joshua to make it harder.','b2',{josh:3},'The flirting becomes unmistakable.'],['Look back and hold Chan’s gaze.','b2',{chan:3},'You test the forbidden rule.'],['Push Joshua into the ocean.','b2',{friend:2},'You buy time with chaos.']]},
b2:{chapter:'DAY FIVE · LIGHTS OUT',place:'BEACH HOUSE KITCHEN · 11:48 PM',who:'Bang Chan',transition:'A summer storm knocks out the power halfway through movie night.',context:'Jihyo and Joshua search for candles. Chan makes ramyeon by flashlight and remembers you hate green onions. When thunder shakes the windows, he reaches for your hand.',text:'Jihyo is my favorite person. I would never hurt her. But pretending I do not notice you is getting difficult.',choices:[['Keep holding his hand.','b3',{chan:4},'The forbidden chemistry becomes real.'],['Tell him Joshua notices you too.','b3',{josh:2},'A flash of jealousy crosses his face.'],['Ask if he would choose the rule over you.','b3',{chan:2,bold:2},'You make him answer honestly.']]},
b3:{chapter:'DAY SEVEN · TELL HER',place:'JIHYO’S BEDROOM · 1:20 AM',who:'Jihyo',transition:'After the bonfire almost ends in a kiss, you wake Jihyo because hiding it feels worse.',context:'She listens to every look, touch, and almost-confession. Then she asks the only question that matters: which one do you actually like?',text:'Do not give me the nice answer. Give me the answer that scares you.',choices:[['“Your brother. I think it has always been Chan.”','b4',{chan:5,confess:1},'She is shocked and hurt you hid it—but listens.'],['“Joshua. I did not expect him.”','b4',{josh:5,confess:1},'She groans, then admits he asks about you constantly.']]},
b4:{chapter:'DAY EIGHT · HER ANSWER',place:'BEACH HOUSE BALCONY · 8:05 AM',who:'Jihyo',transition:'Jihyo takes the night to think. At breakfast, she brings you outside alone.',context:'If you chose Chan, she admits the rule came from fear of losing you both. If you chose Joshua, she warns that his perfect manners disappear when he cares enough to compete.',text:'I do not choose for you. I only demand that if this becomes real, nobody lies to me again.',choices:[['Promise your friendship comes first.','b5',{friend:4},'You protect the first love story in your life.'],['Ask her to plan your confession.','b5',{friend:3,bold:1},'She immediately produces a color-coded plan.']]},
b5:{chapter:'FINALE · THE CHOICE',place:'MOONLIT BEACH · 10:30 PM',who:'You',transition:'Jihyo’s plan ends with fairy lights—and both boys arriving because Sana “misread” one important text.',context:'Chan looks at Joshua. Joshua looks at Chan. Both look at you. Jihyo squeezes your hand and steps away. The boy you confessed about waits near the water.',text:'Your summer has reached the moment you will remember forever.',choices:[['Walk to him and kiss him.','bend',{love:5},'You choose the man you were brave enough to name.'],['Take his hand and ask for a real date.','bend',{slow:5},'You choose a beginning, not a perfect ending.']]}}});

Object.assign(stories[2],{title:'Boyfriend for the Wedding',genre:'Fake Dating · Second Chance',length:'6 scenes · 3 endings',hook:'Your ex is getting married in Jeju. Your celebrity client becomes your fake date. Then your first love arrives.',tags:['fake dating','only one room','first love'],cast:[['V','BTS','Your actor fake boyfriend','Old-soul charm and dangerously convincing affection.'],['Felix','Stray Kids','Your first love and the best man','Sunshine warmth with one unfinished goodbye.'],['Yunjin','LE SSERAFIM','Your manager','Bold, candid, and living for the drama.'],['Kazuha','LE SSERAFIM','The bride’s elegant cousin','Calm observer and unexpected wingwoman.'],['Hanni','NewJeans','Your younger sister','Quick-witted keeper of your oldest secrets.']],setup:{kicker:'FAKE BOYFRIEND. REAL FIRST LOVE. ONE HOTEL ROOM.',title:'Boyfriend for the Wedding',body:'Your ex invites you to his Jeju wedding with the note: “I hope you found someone too.” You have not. Your celebrity client V volunteers to play your boyfriend. The plan is perfect until the best man turns out to be Felix—the first love who left without goodbye.',stakes:'Keep the fake relationship convincing, survive one shared hotel room, and decide whether your heart belongs to the man playing the role or the one who came back.',warning:'A fictional fake-dating romantic comedy. All characters are adults.'},start:'w0',nodes:{
w0:{chapter:'CHAPTER 1 · THE INVITATION',place:'YOUR AGENCY · MONDAY, 6:40 PM',who:'Yunjin',transition:'A cream wedding invitation arrives at work and ruins an excellent Monday.',context:'Yunjin reads your ex’s note with theatrical disgust. V overhears and offers a solution: he needs relationship experience for his next drama, and you need a date nobody will pity.',text:'Three days. I hold your hand, look devastated by your beauty, and make your ex regret having eyes. Strictly professional.',choices:[['Accept with five strict rules.','w1',{v:3},'Rule five: no real feelings. Naturally.'],['Accept only if Yunjin supervises.','w1',{trust:2,v:1},'A witness joins the disaster.'],['Refuse—then your ex texts.','w1',{v:2,bold:1},'Spite changes your mind.']]},
w1:{chapter:'CHAPTER 2 · ARRIVALS',place:'JEJU SEASIDE RESORT · FRIDAY, 3:10 PM',who:'Felix',transition:'V practices pet names on the flight and takes your hand before the car door opens.',context:'The performance works. Your ex looks stunned. Then the best man turns around: Felix, your first love, wearing the expression of someone who rehearsed this reunion for years.',text:'You look happy. I wanted to apologize before the wedding. I just did not know you were bringing him.',choices:[['Introduce V as your boyfriend.','w2',{v:3},'The fake relationship suddenly feels real.'],['Ask Felix to walk later—alone.','w2',{felix:3},'You reopen an unfinished goodbye.'],['Tell both men you need a drink.','w2',{bold:2},'Avoidance, but glamorous.']]},
w2:{chapter:'CHAPTER 2 · ONE ROOM',place:'HONEYMOON SUITE · 5:45 PM',who:'V',transition:'The hotel loses your booking. The only room has one bed and rose petals spelling FOREVER.',context:'V offers to sleep on a four-foot sofa. While you argue, Felix texts asking to meet at the lighthouse. V sees the name, but not the message.',text:'Rule two says we do not lie when we are alone. So tell me whether I am pretending to be jealous.',choices:[['Sit beside V and admit it looks real.','w3',{v:4},'The space between you disappears.'],['Meet Felix at the lighthouse.','w3',{felix:4},'You choose unfinished history.'],['Invite Felix up for honesty.','w3',{truth:3},'One bed becomes the smallest problem.']]},
w3:{chapter:'CHAPTER 3 · REHEARSAL DINNER',place:'CLIFFSIDE TERRACE · 8:30 PM',who:'Hanni',transition:'By dinner, the entire wedding believes the fake relationship—including your sister.',context:'V refills your water and finishes your sentences. Felix plays the song you loved at nineteen. Your ex announces a couples’ dance designed to expose you.',text:'One man knows who you became. The other remembers who you were. Ask where you can breathe.',choices:[['Dance with V and forget the audience.','w4',{v:4},'He misses the cue because he is staring.'],['Ask Felix for the dance you never had.','w4',{felix:4},'He remembers every step.'],['Dance with Hanni and refuse the test.','w4',{self:3},'Your sister saves you with bad choreography.']]},
w4:{chapter:'CHAPTER 3 · THE RAIN SCENE',place:'JEJU LIGHTHOUSE · 11:52 PM',who:'Your chosen man',transition:'A storm ends the dinner. You run to the lighthouse, where one man follows with an umbrella.',context:'There is no audience, ex, or contract here. Only rain, the ocean, and the person your choices kept pulling closer.',text:'Tell me one thing. Was any part of this weekend real?',choices:[['Kiss him in the rain.','w5',{heart:4},'The cliché is perfect for a reason.'],['Tell the whole truth first.','w5',{trust:4},'You choose confession over performance.'],['Ask for one night without labels.','w5',{bold:3},'You choose the present.']]},
w5:{chapter:'FINALE · THE WEDDING',place:'GLASS CHAPEL · SATURDAY, 4:00 PM',who:'Kazuha',transition:'The storm clears. Kazuha returns the fake-dating contract V dropped at the lighthouse.',context:'V has crossed out his signature and written: “After the wedding, ask me again—for real.” Felix waits outside with the letter he wrote when he left. Both finally offer truth instead of timing.',text:'The ceremony is starting. But I think your ending is waiting outside.',choices:[['Find the man your choices favored.','wend',{love:5},'You choose the heart you kept returning to.'],['Leave with Hanni; make them court you.','wend',{self:5},'You choose yourself and a better chapter.'],['Tear up the contract and choose V.','wend',{v:5},'The fake boyfriend gets one real chance.']]}}});

Object.assign(stories[0],{length:'21 scenes · 4 endings',setup:{kicker:'ONE OUTING. THREE MEN. NO SAFE CHOICE.',title:'Three After Midnight',body:'The annual company outing should be harmless: dinner, karaoke, one drink, then home. Instead, your office crush Jungkook, playful strategist San, and intimidating team lead Mingyu spend the entire night competing for your attention—and every little choice makes one of them fall harder.',stakes:'Flirt through dinner, answer three private text conversations, survive a very eventful bar stop, and decide who you trust to take you home after midnight.',warning:'A playful, risqué fictional office romance. Everyone is an adult; intimate endings fade to black.'},start:'d0',nodes:{
d0:{chapter:'CHAPTER 1 · DINNER',place:'HAN RIVER COMPANY OUTING · 7:05 PM',who:'Jennie',transition:'The company outing begins with Korean barbecue at a long private table overlooking the river.',context:'Jennie saves you one seat, but three coworkers arrive at once. Jungkook gives you his shy, hopeful smile. San pulls out a chair with shameless confidence. Mingyu raises an eyebrow as if seating arrangements are a business decision.',text:'Choose carefully. Dinner lasts ninety minutes, and at least two of them are already jealous.',choices:[['Sit beside Jungkook, with San directly across.','d1',{jk:2,san:1},'Jungkook stays close; San gets uninterrupted eye contact.'],['Sit between San and Mingyu.','d1',{san:2,mingyu:2},'Maximum tension and nowhere to hide.'],['Sit beside Mingyu, with Jungkook across from you.','d1',{mingyu:2,jk:1},'Mingyu serves your food; Jungkook watches every bite.']]},
d1:{chapter:'CHAPTER 1 · UNDER THE TABLE',place:'COMPANY DINNER · 7:42 PM',who:'You',transition:'Dinner settles into speeches, sizzling meat, and a quarterly update nobody wanted.',context:'Your chosen seats turn every small movement into a possibility. Jennie is pretending to listen to the director while tracking the romantic geometry around you.',text:'The director begins slide fourteen. You have never been more ready for karaoke.',choices:[['Hold Jungkook’s gaze until he looks away smiling.','d2',{jk:3},'He mouths: “You are distracting me.”'],['Play footsie with San beneath the table.','d2',{san:3,bold:1},'He traps your shoe between his and does not let go.'],['Text Mingyu: “I’m bored. Rescue me at karaoke?”','d2',{mingyu:3},'He replies: “Behave for twenty minutes. Then you are mine.”']]},
d2:{chapter:'CHAPTER 2 · KARAOKE',place:'NEON NOTE KARAOKE · 9:18 PM',who:'Rosé',transition:'Jennie links arms with you on the walk to karaoke. Rosé reaches the song tablet first and immediately starts making teams.',context:'Rosé insists the first round must be duets. All three men volunteer before she finishes explaining. She hands you the microphone and lets you decide.',text:'Pick for talent, chemistry, or chaos. Ideally all three.',choices:[['Choose Jungkook—the strongest singer.','k_jk',{jk:3},'Expect playful vocal banter and a full serenade.'],['Choose San—the best dancer.','k_san',{san:3},'Expect a dance break and a dramatic spin into his arms.'],['Choose Mingyu—the competitive wildcard.','k_mg',{mingyu:3},'He says you will ruin his chance of winning. He is smiling.']]},
k_jk:{chapter:'CHAPTER 2 · THE SERENADE',place:'KARAOKE ROOM 7 · 9:31 PM',who:'Jungkook',transition:'Jungkook chooses a love song, then lowers the key when you accuse him of trying to show off.',context:'You trade lines, deliberately interrupt each other, and make Rosé threaten to deduct points for flirting. During the final chorus, Jungkook stops watching the lyrics and sings directly to you.',text:'I picked the song because it says what I have been too nervous to say at work.',choices:[['Bump his shoulder and finish the harmony.','p0',{jk:2},'Sweet, close, and impossible to misread.'],['Sing the final line inches from his face.','p0',{jk:4,bold:1},'The room erupts before either of you can kiss.']]},
k_san:{chapter:'CHAPTER 2 · THE DANCE BREAK',place:'KARAOKE ROOM 7 · 9:31 PM',who:'San',transition:'San picks the loudest dance track available and promises the choreography is “extremely beginner-friendly.” It is not.',context:'He guides your hips through the first move, laughs when you step on him, then spins you cleanly into his arms for the chorus. You land against his chest while the entire room screams.',text:'See? Perfect. Although I might have forgotten the part where I let you go.',choices:[['Stay in his arms through the next chorus.','p0',{san:4},'He dances closer and forgets everyone else.'],['Spin him back and make him chase you.','p0',{san:2,bold:2},'The performance becomes a flirtatious competition.']]},
k_mg:{chapter:'CHAPTER 2 · THE COMPETITION',place:'KARAOKE ROOM 7 · 9:31 PM',who:'Mingyu',transition:'Mingyu complains that your song choice is too difficult, steals the better microphone, and announces that losing is not an option.',context:'He corrects your entrance, you deliberately sing his line, and the argument becomes the best performance of the night. When the score flashes 98, he lifts you off the floor in celebration before remembering he is your boss.',text:'You did not ruin my chances. Do not look so pleased—I am still taking most of the credit.',choices:[['Tell him the lift deserves a bonus.','p0',{mingyu:4},'His hands linger at your waist.'],['Demand a rematch—with higher stakes.','p0',{mingyu:2,bold:2},'He quietly asks what you want to wager.']]},
p0:{chapter:'CHAPTER 2 · THREE MEN ARE TYPING',place:'THREE PRIVATE CONVERSATIONS · 10:14 PM',who:'Your phone',transition:'Jennie drags you into the hallway to cool down. Three messages arrive before the karaoke door closes.',context:'Each man thinks he has your attention. For the next five minutes, he does. Reply separately to all three conversations; every answer changes his love meter.',type:'triple-phone',next:'m0',phoneChats:{jk:{name:'Jungkook',initial:'You were beautiful up there. Was the flirting part of the performance?',options:[['“Maybe I need a private encore.”','Then I know a quieter place. Just say when.',3],['“You were the one serenading me.”','I have been trying to do that for months.',2],['“Focus, superstar. We have coworkers.”','I noticed. I only cared whether you noticed me.',1]]},san:{name:'San',initial:'I give our chemistry a 10. The judges were cowards.',options:[['“Your hands seemed very confident.”','They would be even more confident without an audience.',3],['“You still owe me a proper dance.”','After the bar. One song, no one else.',2],['“I nearly fell!”','I knew I would catch you. I always will.',1]]},mingyu:{name:'Mingyu',initial:'You disappeared before I could collect my prize.',options:[['“What prize did you have in mind, boss?”','Ask me after one drink. I will stop pretending to be professional.',3],['“A rematch. Loser buys breakfast.”','Deal. I intend to choose the breakfast place.',2],['“You already took all the credit.”','Not for the part I actually wanted.',1]]}}},
m0:{chapter:'CHAPTER 3 · THE SPILLED DRINK',place:'VELVET ROOM BAR · 10:52 PM',who:'Mingyu',transition:'The team moves to a quiet cocktail bar. Mingyu orders your usual before you reach the counter.',context:'A coworker bumps your elbow. The drink spills down your sleeve and across Mingyu’s jacket. He checks your hand for glass, guides you away from the crowd, and slips off his clean overshirt.',text:'Wear this. That is not a manager request—it is me trying very hard to take care of you.',choices:[['Accept his jacket and let him clean your wrist.','j0',{mingyu:4},'His touch is careful; the eye contact is not.'],['Accept it, then hug him in thanks.','j0',{mingyu:5,bold:1},'He freezes before wrapping both arms around you.'],['Refuse gently and clean up yourself.','j0',{mingyu:1},'He respects the boundary but still waits nearby.']]},
j0:{chapter:'CHAPTER 3 · THE MOTORCYCLE',place:'BAR SERVICE ALLEY · 11:13 PM',who:'Jungkook',transition:'You head toward the bathroom to finish cleaning up and find Jungkook waiting beside the back exit.',context:'He offers fresh air instead of a cigarette and leads you to his motorcycle beneath the alley lights. He places his spare helmet in your hands, then fastens the strap beneath your chin when your fingers fumble.',text:'I am not asking you to leave. I just wanted five minutes where nobody else was competing.',choices:[['Climb on for one slow trip around the block.','s0x',{jk:4},'You hold his waist; he takes the longest route possible.'],['Stay by the bike and kiss his cheek.','s0x',{jk:3,bold:1},'He turns at the last second; the kiss nearly lands elsewhere.'],['Return the helmet but ask him to wait for you.','s0x',{jk:2,trust:1},'A promise can be more intimate than a ride.']]},
s0x:{chapter:'CHAPTER 3 · CAUGHT',place:'VELVET ROOM DANCE FLOOR · 11:41 PM',who:'San',transition:'Back inside, you finish the safe half of your drink. The music and the long evening leave you pleasantly unsteady.',context:'Your heel catches as you cross the dance floor. San catches you at the waist before you fall. One hand braces your back; the other holds yours. Neither of you moves.',text:'Careful. If you wanted to end up in my arms, you could have just asked.',choices:[['Stay there and dance against him.','team',{san:5},'He holds you close through an entire slow song.'],['Loop your arms around him in a lingering hug.','team',{san:3,trust:1},'His teasing softens into something tender.'],['Step back, then blow him a kiss.','team',{san:2,bold:1},'You leave him wanting more.']]},
team:{chapter:'CHAPTER 4 · LAST CALL',place:'VELVET ROOM · 12:18 AM',who:'Jennie',transition:'Jennie calls an emergency team meeting when the company director begins ordering shots for everyone.',context:'Taxis are called. Coats are collected. Jungkook has his helmet, San has an umbrella, and Mingyu already has the ride-share app open. All three offer to take you home.',text:'Choose your ride. But fair warning: the man who fell hardest tonight may not let the evening end that easily.',routeByLove:true,choices:[['Ask Jungkook to take you home.','h_jk',{},'Motorcycle or taxi—he promises to get you there safely.','jk'],['Ask San to take you home.','h_san',{},'He promises midnight food and no boring route.','san'],['Ask Mingyu to take you home.','h_mingyu',{},'He has water, a car, and a very convincing serious face.','mingyu'],['Leave together as a group.','fend',{friends:5},'A warm, chaotic ending with breakfast for everyone.','all']]},
h_jk:{chapter:'FINALE · YOUR DOOR',place:'OUTSIDE YOUR APARTMENT · 1:02 AM',who:'Jungkook',transition:'Jungkook gets you home safely, his jacket around your shoulders and your hands linked inside one pocket.',context:'At your door, he removes one loose strand of hair from your face and waits. He will not assume the night continues—but he is hoping.',text:'I can say goodnight. Or you can ask me to stay, and I will make breakfast in the morning.',choices:[['Invite him in for a steamy night.','oend',{stay:5},'The door closes. The rest belongs to you.'],['Invite him in for tea and a quiet cuddle.','oend',{slow:5},'Intimate, warm, and unhurried.'],['Kiss him goodnight and go inside alone.','oend',{reject:5},'You keep the spark without making a promise.']]},
h_san:{chapter:'FINALE · YOUR DOOR',place:'OUTSIDE YOUR APARTMENT · 1:02 AM',who:'San',transition:'San walks you home beneath one umbrella, taking every detour that keeps your shoulders touching.',context:'At your door, he rests one hand against the wall beside you and asks before moving any closer. The playful smile is gone; the desire is not.',text:'Tell me to leave and I will. Tell me to stay and I promise you will remember tonight.',choices:[['Invite him in for a steamy night.','oend',{stay:5},'The door closes. The rest belongs to you.'],['Invite him in for food and a movie.','oend',{slow:5},'Flirting melts into a soft, sleepy night.'],['Kiss him once and say goodnight.','oend',{reject:5},'He leaves smiling—and texts from the elevator.']]},
h_mingyu:{chapter:'FINALE · YOUR DOOR',place:'OUTSIDE YOUR APARTMENT · 1:02 AM',who:'Mingyu',transition:'Mingyu’s car is warm and quiet. He walks you to the door carrying your bag and the shoes you gave up on halfway home.',context:'He sets everything down but keeps hold of his jacket around your shoulders. For once, your team lead has no instruction—only a question.',text:'At work, I have to be careful. Here, I only need to know what you want.',choices:[['Pull him inside for a steamy night.','oend',{stay:5},'The door closes. The rest belongs to you.'],['Invite him in for tea and honest conversation.','oend',{slow:5},'The demanding boss becomes unexpectedly tender.'],['Return his jacket and kiss him goodnight.','oend',{reject:5},'Tomorrow’s office tension will be spectacular.']]},
fend:{chapter:'FRIENDLY ENDING · BREAKFAST',place:'24-HOUR DINER · 1:11 AM',who:'Jennie',transition:'You refuse to choose a private ride, so Jennie reroutes everyone to a twenty-four-hour diner.',context:'Jungkook steals fries from your plate. San orders for the table. Mingyu makes everyone drink water. The competition pauses long enough to become genuine friendship.',text:'Honestly? Making all three of them wait might be your most powerful move tonight.',choices:[['End the night with pancakes and possibilities.','oend',{chaos:5},'No heartbreak. No winner. Not yet.']]}}});

